            <ArticleTitle>[Hemorheologic indices of patients with chronic ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors examined 35 patients suffering from ischemic heart disease with signs of stage-I circulatory insufficiency. It was established that the hemorheological values were distinctly increased. This increase was associated with an increase of the general peripheral resistance.</AbstractText>
